Z||000011||hugh||11-20-2001||08:02 PM||||The GN is a 231 cubic inch off center V6 engine.With the turbo it was rated 225 horsepower stock.The GNX was pulled from the GN assembly line and modified by an outside company(whose name escapes me).There were 547GNX cars.They had a much better straight line suspension.Different turbo,cosmetics.My GN has stage one heads,which gives slightly better cylinder sealing because of the thicker head surface.They have had some port work.My engine internals are stock,except for a Reed cam(cam is not as important in a turbo).At the time I ran 12.2@115 it had the stock 3.43 rear,stock headers,bigger injectors,stock throttle body,Spearco intercooler,modified front bumper(more air flow),trans shift kit.I had 26"x10" slicks and couldn't get the car moving because of tire spin through 1st and 2nd gears(1.95 60').This was because it needed new front springs and was too low in front(no weight transfer).Now I have a bigger turbo and SS exhaust system that came off my brothers T Type,bigger throttle body,3.89 9" Ford rear.What the car did before computes to 441 HP,which is at the ragged edge for the head gaskets,as they only have 4 bolts per cylinder.This is my daily driver.There have been some Fieros done with a GN engine,I don't know how the transmission holds up to all that torque.I would love to put an engine like mine in a Fiero WOW!!!!  <BR>The 3800 is an on center engine.<BR>OH,I also get over 20 MPG on the highway!||||reg||14
Z||000012||avengador1||11-20-2001||08:03 PM||||The car was so fast that I even saw a Corvette owner swap out his V-8 for the GNX engine and had his car in the 10's.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Wannabe||11-20-2001||08:12 PM||||An "Anniversary Edition" Trans Am was also offered with this engine - in '89 I think. It ran mid 13's out of the box. Car& Driver tested one of the first intercooled GN's on a very cold day and published some unheard of for stock 1/4 mile times, significantly faster than the Corvette of the same year. They estimated the engine was putting out around 290 hp, as compared to the factory's rating closer to 235 - I don't recall the exact figure. All in all, a very nice surprise from Buick back in the '80s.||||reg||1
Z||000014||hugh||11-20-2001||08:18 PM||||Actually the Trans Am turbo engine had slightly better heads because the narrower frame rails caused the engineers to change the exhaust ports to narrow the engine.They gave the exhaust a straighter shot out of the cylinders.||||reg||14
